@startuml sequence_diagram_kitchen_viewer
autonumber
title WEB01 - UC3: view the active kitchen in the shared shell

actor "Restaurant Staff or Manager" as User
participant "Kitchen viewer (VIS01)" as Viewer
participant "kitchenConfigurationApi (WEB06)" as Adapter
participant ModuleRequest as Request
participant apiClient as Client
participant "Back-End API" as API

ref over User, API : SD3 - Open the viewer in the shared shell; continue only if mounted
note over Viewer, API
Proposed integration. WEB06 owns the endpoint and JSON contract (OP1).
The back end authorises each protected operation.
end note

Viewer -> Adapter : getActive()
Adapter -> Request : request(GET, active-configuration path)
Request -> Client : request(GET, path, { accessToken })
Client -> API : Read active kitchen configuration (Bearer)
alt Active configuration returned
  API --> Client : DTO with configuration ID, JSON and asset references
  Client --> Request : Parsed DTO
  Request --> Adapter : DTO
  Adapter --> Viewer : DTO
  alt 3D rendering available
    Viewer --> User : Render the active layout in the same SPA
  else WebGL unavailable
    Viewer --> User : Explain why the scene cannot be displayed
  end
else No active configuration or request failed
  opt API sent an error response
    API --> Client : HTTP error
  end
  Client --> Request : ApiError
  ref over Request, API : Protected error rule (SD3)
  Request --> Adapter : Original ApiError
  Adapter --> Viewer : ApiError
  Viewer --> User : Explain failure; no embedded layout is substituted
end
@enduml
